      "writtenOn": "2019-02-13T20:35:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A platform with a real ion implementation/use shouldn\u0027t be hijacking the \u0027dummy_driver\u0027 backend. This code didn\u0027t even exist in older kernels. This implementation exhaustively defines all heaps - and if the system doesn\u0027t use one or more of them, it\u0027s just opening itself up to wasted memory and increased attack surface.",
